{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981199-help-me-understand-2e-blood-sorcery","id":981199,"title":"Help Me Understand 2e Blood Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T19:14:19-07:00","id":981199,"title":"Help Me Understand 2e Blood Sorcery","content":"The potency of a ritual like Touch of the Morrigan is defined as &quot;1 + 1 per success rolled above the target&quot;, but The Request rules state that 'once the number of successes is met, the ritual\u2019s effect immediately takes place&quot;.<br /> <br /> This got me confused. Let's assume a vampire has 6 dice on her dice pool. She will roll 6 times. What happens?<br /> <br /> 1) if the vampire gets the target number of successes (six) in two rolls, does she keep rolling until all EIGHT rolls are done? Example: First two rolls get 3 successes each, and the other 4 rolls all add to Potency?<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> 2) if the vampire gets the target number of successes (six) in two rolls, does she stop rolling and prays for overlapping successes? Example: First roll gets 3 successes, second roll gets 5. Is the damage 3?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":11263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","user":"Gimmisky","date":". 10-04-2016, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T22:27:15-07:00","id":981275,"title":"","content":"Extended actions are finished once you reach or exceed the target successes, so 2 is the correct scenario. With Blood Sorcery, the Discipline rating is part of the pool, not a special modifier; you'd get ten dice in your hypothetical .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:57:20-07:00","id":981299,"title":"","content":"2 is the correct answer, which is pretty dumb in the case of rituals like Touch of the Morrigan. The problem is that they directly ported the sample rituals from the 1e core book to 2e without accounting for the fact that blood sorcery worked in a matter of turns in 1e instead of a matter of hours. I would recommend either Blood Sorcery: Sacrements and Blasphemies, and either use the creative casting system from that, or just using it to create new rituals. For a quick and dirty fix, just allow players with blood sorcery to set the Potency ahead of time, with each additional Potency increasing the required Successes by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:35:29-07:00","id":981376,"title":"","content":"Or keep the 1ed system of rituals taking turns instead of hours. I'm not sure why they did that whole hours thing. It makes them really hard to use unless you plan far ahead. I gave the opportunity to one of my players to learn some Theban Sorcery and he took the blood scourge and the damage upgrade curse. He already forgets to use them most of the time, but given that the players are very busy and encounter a lot of unexpected stuff, he would almost never be able to use them if they took hours to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:58:59-07:00","id":981404,"title":"","content":"There's a theban sorcery ritual that is so inefficient that it would literally be easier and more effective to just stab the victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T06:57:15-07:00","id":981417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981199-help-me-understand-2e-blood-sorcery?p=981376#post981376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or keep the 1ed system of rituals taking turns instead of hours. I'm not sure why they did that whole hours thing. It makes them really hard to use unless you plan far ahead. I gave the opportunity to one of my players to learn some Theban Sorcery and he took the blood scourge and the damage upgrade curse. He already forgets to use them most of the time, but given that the players are very busy and encounter a lot of unexpected stuff, he would almost never be able to use them if they took hours to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was mostly used to balance the system from Blood Sorcery book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That one was fairly broken with turns. <br /> Using the casting rules from 2ed book with the ritual rules from the Blood Sorcery book provides the best result in my opinion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}